sha256.c/sha256.h started as Igor Pavlov's public domain Sha256.c (LZMA SDK),
based on public domain code from Wei Dai's Crypto++. Marc Bevand's changes to
it are under SILENTARMY's license above.

The file in zebrad/ is a patch to Zcash Crosslink
(https://github.com/ShieldedLabs/crosslink_monolith), not part of metal-eq.
zebrad/zebrad-gpu-solvers-v18.patch changes zebrad (zebra-crosslink, licensed
MIT OR Apache-2.0). The changes it makes are offered under the MIT license
above or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at your option. The upstream code it
shows (diff context) belongs to its authors and stays under upstream's terms.
